+PAL_arafat_dead_TT: "§HYasser Arafat§! dies"
+
+ # Israeli OEM Landscape
+ ISR_oem_specialized_electronics_export_base: "Specialized Electronics Export Base"
+ ISR_oem_specialized_electronics_export_base_desc: "Israel's industrial strength lies in carrier equipment, satellite terminals, digital presses, production equipment, storage devices, and other high-value niches rather than mass consumer electronics."
+ ISR_oem_defense_civilian_spillover: "Defense–Civilian Technology Spillover"
+ ISR_oem_defense_civilian_spillover_desc: "Military demand for sensors, communications, optics, avionics, and secure computing feeds skills and technology into the civilian electronics sector."
+ ISR_oem_foreign_acquisition_magnet: "Foreign-Acquisition Magnet"
+ ISR_oem_foreign_acquisition_magnet_desc: "Israeli firms attract venture funding, multinational partnerships, and premium acquisition offers. Capital and market access arrive quickly, but domestic ownership is difficult to preserve."
+ ISR_oem_fragmented_industrial_champions: "Fragmented Industrial Champions"
+ ISR_oem_fragmented_industrial_champions_desc: "A dense field of specialized exporters possesses formidable engineering talent but limited conglomerate scale, duplicated overhead, and exposure to narrow market cycles."
+ ISR_oem_startup_nation_network: "Startup Nation Network"
+ ISR_oem_startup_nation_network_desc: "Venture capital, public listings, foreign strategic partners, and serial entrepreneurship connect Israeli specialists to global markets. Liquidity and innovation thrive even as successful firms remain vulnerable to acquisition."
+ ISR_oem_national_champions: "National Champions"
+ ISR_oem_national_champions_desc: "Public finance, procurement, and patient domestic capital support independent Israeli firms in capital-intensive markets. Sovereign capability comes at a meaningful fiscal and efficiency cost."
+ ISR_oem_strategic_consolidation: "Strategic Consolidation"
+ ISR_oem_strategic_consolidation_desc: "Telecommunications, printing, semiconductor equipment, and defense electronics are organized around fewer, broader groups. Scale improves, while integration friction and weaker competition exact a price."
+
+ ISR_oem_startup_nation_bonus: "Startup-Network Research"
+ ISR_oem_national_champions_bonus: "National-Champion Research"
+ ISR_oem_strategic_consolidation_bonus: "Consolidated-Industry Research"
+
+ ISR_oem_events.1.t: "ECI: Carrier-Equipment Champion"
+ ISR_oem_events.1.d: "ECI entered 2000 as Israel's clearest civilian telecommunications champion. Its 1999 absorption of Tadiran Telecommunications was already complete, leaving the combined group to sell broadband access, optical transport, cross-connect, and data-networking systems into a surging global carrier market. The question is whether ECI should remain an export-led specialist, receive national backing, or anchor a broader domestic consolidation."
+ ISR_oem_events.1.a: "Let ECI ride the carrier boom"
+ ISR_oem_events.1.a_tt: "ECI will compete for global carrier orders.\nThe §YStartup Nation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nGain §G10§! Political Power and a §G10%§! research bonus for §YInternet Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.1.b: "Back a civilian national champion"
+ ISR_oem_events.1.b_tt: "Procurement policy will reinforce ECI as an independent Israeli carrier-equipment champion.\nThe §YNational Champions§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R10§! Political Power and gain a §G15%§! research bonus for §YInternet Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.1.c: "Consolidate the telecom houses"
+ ISR_oem_events.1.c_tt: "Policy will encourage ECI, Telrad, and the RAD ecosystem to coordinate around a broader communications group.\nThe §YStrategic Consolidation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R15§! Political Power, gain §G0.5%§! Stability, and gain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YInternet§! or §YComputing Technology§!."
+
+ ISR_oem_events.2.t: "Indigo: HP Courts Indigo"
+ ISR_oem_events.2.d: "Indigo manufactures complete digital color presses, making it one of Israel's purest industrial-equipment OEMs. Hewlett-Packard has offered a $100 million strategic investment, joint development, and an OEM partnership. The alliance promises distribution and capital without yet surrendering Indigo's independence, but it could become the first step toward foreign ownership."
+ ISR_oem_events.2.a: "Accept HP's investment and OEM pact"
+ ISR_oem_events.2.a_tt: "HP capital and distribution will accelerate Indigo's global reach.\nThe §YStartup Nation§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §G+$1.00 billion§!\nGain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YComputing Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.2.b: "Finance an independent global scale-up"
+ ISR_oem_events.2.b_tt: "Public capital will keep Indigo independent while it expands abroad.\nThe §YNational Champions§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §R-$3.00 billion§!\nGain a §G15%§! research bonus for §YComputing Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.2.c: "Assemble an Israeli digital-printing group"
+ ISR_oem_events.2.c_tt: "Indigo will become the center of a domestic printing-equipment group.\nThe §YStrategic Consolidation§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §R-$2.00 billion§!\nGain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YComputing§! or §YInternet Technology§!."
+
+ ISR_oem_events.3.t: "M-Systems: The DiskOnKey"
+ ISR_oem_events.3.d: "M-Systems already sells DiskOnChip embedded flash and rugged FFD storage, but its new DiskOnKey turns solid-state memory into a removable USB product. It is a device maker rather than a semiconductor foundry, and its opportunity lies in deciding whether this invention should scale through global OEMs, sovereign standards, or rugged industrial markets."
+ ISR_oem_events.3.a: "Partner with IBM and global OEMs"
+ ISR_oem_events.3.a_tt: "Global partners will take DiskOnKey rapidly into commercial markets.\nThe §YStartup Nation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nGain §G5§! Political Power and a §G10%§! research bonus for §YComputing§! or §YMicrochip Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.3.b: "Fund an Israeli storage standard"
+ ISR_oem_events.3.b_tt: "The state will sponsor an independent flash-storage platform.\nThe §YNational Champions§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R15§! Political Power and gain a §G15%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.3.c: "Tie flash storage to defense and industry"
+ ISR_oem_events.3.c_tt: "Rugged embedded storage will connect M-Systems to domestic systems integrators.\nThe §YStrategic Consolidation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nGain §G0.5%§! Stability and a §G10%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip§! or §YInternet Technology§!."
+
+ ISR_oem_events.4.t: "Tower: Finance Fab 2"
+ ISR_oem_events.4.d: "Tower Semiconductor operates Israel's indigenous 150 mm Fab 1 as an independent foundry. Its proposed 200 mm Fab 2 would be a capital-intensive expansion financed over years, not instant productive capacity. The government must choose between foreign partners, sovereign guarantees, or a smaller program centered on Fab 1 and the surrounding equipment cluster."
+ ISR_oem_events.4.a: "Bring in foreign strategic partners"
+ ISR_oem_events.4.a_tt: "Foreign partners will share the risk and financing of the Fab 2 cycle.\nThe §YStartup Nation§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §R-$2.00 billion§!\nGain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip Technology§!.\n§LNo fabrication plant is added by this financing decision.§!"
+ ISR_oem_events.4.b: "Guarantee a sovereign Fab 2 program"
+ ISR_oem_events.4.b_tt: "The state will assume the financial risk of preserving indigenous wafer capacity.\nThe §YNational Champions§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §R-$6.00 billion§!\nGain a §G15%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip Technology§!.\n§LNo fabrication plant is added by this financing decision.§!"
+ ISR_oem_events.4.c: "Phase the expansion around Fab 1"
+ ISR_oem_events.4.c_tt: "Tower, Nova, Camtek, and Orbotech will coordinate a lower-risk capacity program.\nThe §YStrategic Consolidation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R10§! Political Power and gain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip§! or §YConstruction Technology§!.\n§LNo fabrication plant is added by this policy decision.§!"
+
+ ISR_oem_events.5.t: "Gilat: Satellite Internet Fever"
+ ISR_oem_events.5.d: "Gilat is a manufacturer of VSAT terminals, hubs, and ground equipment as well as an integrator of turnkey satellite networks. The dot-com boom has made consumer satellite broadband appear within reach, but enterprise systems, rural connectivity, and critical communications offer slower and more disciplined alternatives."
+ ISR_oem_events.5.a: "Chase the consumer broadband market"
+ ISR_oem_events.5.a_tt: "Gilat will pursue the high-risk consumer satellite opportunity.\nThe §YStartup Nation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R0.5%§! Stability and gain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YSpace Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.5.b: "Prioritize rural and public networks"
+ ISR_oem_events.5.b_tt: "Public-network contracts will favor disciplined deployment over speculative scale.\nThe §YNational Champions§! path gains §G1§! point.\nGain §G0.5%§! Stability and a §G10%§! research bonus for §YSpace§! or §YInternet Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.5.c: "Integrate critical-communications suppliers"
+ ISR_oem_events.5.c_tt: "Gilat's terminals will be coordinated with Israel's broader communications sector.\nThe §YStrategic Consolidation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R10§! Political Power and gain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YSpace§! or §YInternet Technology§!."
+
+ ISR_oem_events.6.t: "Scitex: The CreoScitex Transaction"
+ ISR_oem_events.6.d: "Creo has agreed to acquire Scitex's digital-prepress assets and combine them in CreoScitex. The April 2000 transaction offers capital and access to a larger international platform, but it also transfers a celebrated Israeli industrial-imaging business abroad. Retention or domestic consolidation would demand public support."
+ ISR_oem_events.6.a: "Approve the CreoScitex transaction"
+ ISR_oem_events.6.a_tt: "The prepress assets will move into an international platform.\nThe §YStartup Nation§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §G+$2.00 billion§!\nGain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YComputing Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.6.b: "Retain Scitex's prepress assets"
+ ISR_oem_events.6.b_tt: "Public backing will preserve an independent Israeli imaging-equipment company.\nThe §YNational Champions§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §R-$2.00 billion§!\nGain a §G15%§! research bonus for §YComputing Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.6.c: "Build a domestic printing group"
+ ISR_oem_events.6.c_tt: "Scitex, Indigo, and NUR will be encouraged to share a domestic industrial platform.\nThe §YStrategic Consolidation§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §R-$1.00 billion§!\nGain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YComputing§! or §YMicrochip Technology§!."
+
+ ISR_oem_events.7.t: "BreezeCOM/Floware: Create Alvarion"
+ ISR_oem_events.7.d: "BreezeCOM and Floware remain separate Israeli broadband-wireless equipment makers until their planned August 2001 combination. A merger would create Alvarion and give the fixed-wireless sector greater scale, while continued rivalry might preserve competition or a state-backed champion could pursue a more directed strategy."
+ ISR_oem_events.7.a: "Keep two wireless challengers"
+ ISR_oem_events.7.a_tt: "BreezeCOM and Floware will remain competing entrepreneurial firms.\nThe §YStartup Nation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nGain §G10§! Political Power and a §G10%§! research bonus for §YInternet Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.7.b: "Designate a protected wireless champion"
+ ISR_oem_events.7.b_tt: "The stronger firm will receive procurement support as a national wireless champion.\nThe §YNational Champions§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R15§! Political Power and gain a §G15%§! research bonus for §YInternet Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.7.c: "Merge them into Alvarion"
+ ISR_oem_events.7.c_tt: "The two systems vendors will combine as Alvarion.\nThe §YStrategic Consolidation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R10§! Political Power and gain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YInternet§! or §YComputing Technology§!."
+
+ ISR_oem_events.8.t: "Galileo: Marvell Moves for Galileo"
+ ISR_oem_events.8.d: "Marvell has offered stock for Galileo Technology, an Israeli designer of networking and switching silicon. Galileo is a fabless semiconductor firm, not a domestic fabrication plant; the choice concerns ownership, design capability, and local research rather than factory capacity."
+ ISR_oem_events.8.a: "Approve the Marvell acquisition"
+ ISR_oem_events.8.a_tt: "Galileo's shareholders will accept the foreign exit.\nThe §YStartup Nation§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §G+$1.00 billion§!\nGain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.8.b: "Sponsor an Israeli counterbid"
+ ISR_oem_events.8.b_tt: "Domestic capital will attempt to keep Galileo independent.\nThe §YNational Champions§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §R-$2.00 billion§!\nGain a §G15%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.8.c: "Bind the deal to a local design cluster"
+ ISR_oem_events.8.c_tt: "Approval will require durable Israeli research links across the communications sector.\nThe §YStrategic Consolidation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nGain §G0.5%§! Stability and a §G10%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip§! or §YInternet Technology§!."
+
+ ISR_oem_events.9.t: "Elbit/El-Op: A Private Defense Champion"
+ ISR_oem_events.9.d: "Elbit Systems and El-Op are preparing a merger that will join avionics, C4I, military computers, sensors, and electro-optics in Israel's largest non-government-owned defense company. The state can preserve supplier competition, complete a bounded national-champion merger, or turn Elbit into the platform for wider private defense consolidation."
+ ISR_oem_events.9.a: "Preserve competition among suppliers"
+ ISR_oem_events.9.a_tt: "El-Op will remain independent and compete for contracts.\nThe §YStartup Nation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nGain §G5§! Political Power and a §G10%§! research bonus for §YComputing§! or §YInternet Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.9.b: "Complete the bounded merger"
+ ISR_oem_events.9.b_tt: "Elbit and El-Op will combine as a private Israeli defense champion.\nThe §YNational Champions§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R10§! Political Power and gain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YComputing§! or §YInternet Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.9.c: "Make Elbit the consolidation platform"
+ ISR_oem_events.9.c_tt: "Procurement policy will prepare Elbit for broader integration of private defense-electronics suppliers.\nThe §YStrategic Consolidation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R20§! Political Power and §R0.5%§! Stability, and gain a §G15%§! research bonus for §YComputing§! or §YInternet Technology§!."
+
+ ISR_oem_events.10.t: "Mellanox: The Interconnect Bet"
+ ISR_oem_events.10.d: "Mellanox began operations only in March 1999. It is an early fabless interconnect startup, not yet a mature data-center champion or a source of domestic fabrication capacity. A modest decision now could give its engineers patient venture backing, a sovereign research mandate, or a place inside a broader communications cluster."
+ ISR_oem_events.10.a: "Supply patient venture capital"
+ ISR_oem_events.10.a_tt: "A small early investment will let Mellanox prove its interconnect designs over time.\nThe §YStartup Nation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R5§! Political Power and gain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip§! or §YInternet Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.10.b: "Commission a sovereign interconnect program"
+ ISR_oem_events.10.b_tt: "The state will fund a long-horizon domestic interconnect capability.\nThe §YNational Champions§! path gains §G1§! point.\n§YTreasury§!: §R-$1.00 billion§!\nGain a §G15%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip Technology§!."
+ ISR_oem_events.10.c: "Embed Mellanox in the systems cluster"
+ ISR_oem_events.10.c_tt: "Mellanox will coordinate its designs with communications and defense integrators.\nThe §YStrategic Consolidation§! path gains §G1§! point.\nLose §R10§! Political Power and gain a §G10%§! research bonus for §YMicrochip§! or §YInternet Technology§!".

